ady in his fifties it is  reversed  and he's given a proper military  discharge and is able to collect his  pension but he's never able to go back  to serving in the Army as he would have  liked he got some kind of low-grade job  in the Department of Agriculture  probably through influence he was from  Iowa he was connected with people who  had credentials there so he got this  bureaucratic job and clearly was not  very happy with it lived the rest of his  life in Washington DC you know what can  I say yes well today most of our  military court marshals are heavily  covered by the press I'm just curious I  know the subject is taboo at this time  and they're in a remote location where  the president ever involved in covering  this case after the case was decided the  Gettys ever go to the press no probably  because he felt it was in his best  interest to try to work within the  system particularly because he was  immediately reinstated and I think he  naively thought that was the end of it  and as far as I know he never went to  the press because he kept working to try  to get back into the army and that  certainly would have been fatal I don't  know how this was kept from the press  except for the fact that there's such a  taboo against incest that it's like that  time that some of us can remember when  the press did not report on the  extracurricular activities of  politicians there was just an unspoken  agreement nothing appeared on San  Antonio where the trial took place was  not that much of a backwater it was at  that time the largest city and the  center of the military department of  Texas nevertheless nothing appeared in  the newspapers  the San Antonio newspapers and there was  a little tiny reference to the trial in  the Army and Navy journal but it was it  just said the the subject matter of the  trial was so vulgar  it couldn't be talked about and in fact  when the army published its abstract of  the trial there was always a printed  abstract that told the basic findings of  a court-martial under these  specifications where they usually say  precisely what happened  it said not fit to be specified that was  the original title of my book which the  editor changed but I was really struck  by that because ordinarily in a  court-martial you have the charge  conduct unbecoming an officer and a  gentleman  and then the specification is on  such-and-such a date this is what he did  that was conduct unbecoming and they  weren't even going to put in print what  he did so society at that time was just  not ready to deal with an incendiary  subject like incest and I think one of  the reasons why I wanted to show this  photo if you can see it of this is  general the Civil War general Ord and  his wife and at that time nine-year-old  daughter and if you'll notice general  orden his daughter form one unit on one  side of the table  mrs. Ord is on the other and the  daughter and Ord at the time of the  trial had this daughter who was the  apple of his eye she was then about the  age of Lily or woman so he could relate  very strongly as a father she's leaning  against him you know in a pose that if  she were older would be seductive I mean  even notice that one shoulder is bare in  the picture now interestingly enough in  the trial testimony there's a very  similar theme reported with lieutenant  or lemon and his daughter in an army  ambulance that's taking them from Fort  Stockton to Fort Davis which was the  day's journey  Lily evidently leaned against her  father's shoulder and he put his arm  around her and it was at this time that  other occupants of the  ambulance noticed that he was actually  touching her breast which one of the  fascinating things to me about this is  that although no one knows anything  scientific about incest at the time it's  not mentioned it's not talked about  people weren't even supposed to think  about it all of the behavior of  lieutenant or woman falls into a very  classic pattern of the incest father as  we've come to know of him in research  that started in the 1970s for example he  was a German immigrant who came from a  much more strongly patriarchal culture  than existed in America at that time and  the incest father often feels very  possessive towards his daughter and I  think when lieutenant or woman is  recklessly we might say putting his hand  on Lily's breast in front of other  people he's asserting his ownership of  her there's another witness who  testified that he overheard a  conversation in which lieutenant or  woman was reproaching Lily with having  had relations with some younger officers  which as far as we know she hadn't done  and again it's like a kind of jealousy  you belong to me you know I'm not going  to let you have a boyfriend which in  fact Lily said during the trial that she  and her father had had an argument about  her getting attentions from younger  officers also incest families tend to be  ones with large numbers of children in  which the wife has a somewhat doesn't  have any authority and that would really  apply to the oralin family as well so I  think there's just everything says to me  that this was an actual case of of  incest  any more questions we finished ready for  signing sure thank you very much  one last thing people often ask me if  this could happen today and I certainly  hope it couldn't that you know the the  military has had trials of sexual  harassment my feeling is that they would  not be as squeamish now about such a  things I don't think you know which is  good news
 

